# `__PACKAGE_NAME__`

Native reply validation must also become a named invalid-response error. In the
qualified rc.117, an invalid RPC payload can arrive as a SchemaError defect.
The private client marks failure only inside the native exit reply codec's
decoder, then translates that marker to its named invalid-response error. It
keeps the native Schemas, Ndjson parser, Protocol and client. It never treats
every SchemaError as a bad reply: transport and request-encoding defects retain
their original identity, and caller interruption remains interruption. Tests
cover bad native replies and an unrelated adapter SchemaError for both reads.
Requalify the cached exit Schema identity and decoder behaviour on Effect
upgrades before retaining or removing this small compatibility handling.

Effect RPC transport over `__DOMAIN_PACKAGE__`. `__DOMAIN_SYMBOL__` policy remains in the
domain service; this package owns the RPC contract, handlers, clients, and HTTP
mounting.

## Exports

- `./group`: public RPC contract group.
- `./handlers`: server handler Layer.
- `./service`: public RPC client service contract.
- `./server`: HTTP/RPC server composition.
- `./live`: production client Layer.
- `./test`: deterministic in-process test Layer.

## Documentation impact

Public RPC changes update the repository transport architecture owner and
affected critical journeys/proof in the same slice.

## Runbook applicability

Provider operations, authority, and runbooks remain repository-owned. Add or
update a target-owned runbook only when an operation or deployment changes.

## Non-claims

This package makes no deployment, provider-state, network-reachability, or
packed-publisher claim.

The client implements the existing domain service and preserves its checked
error vocabulary. The caller supplies its checked stage API origin and native
HttpClient. Each complete read has one domain-owned deadline; no automatic retry.
